# Force LF on checkout for tracked text files, regardless of platform or
# whatever core.autocrlf a contributor's (or CI runner's) git has —
# GitHub-hosted Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, which was
# silently checking out .ts sources and test fixtures with CRLF and
# breaking round-trip/byte-for-byte tests that compare against a hardcoded
# `\n`-only expectation. Binary assets are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
